note right of BlackboxBackend
  Implements the base contract only, so it
  answers no capability. A step whose
  capability no backend in the scenario's
  order provides throws
  UnsupportedBackendActionException.
end note

note bottom of DrupalBackendInterface
  DrupalBackendInterface extends 33 capability
  interfaces and DrushBackendInterface 13, of
  which DrushCapabilityInterface is its own.
  Both backend classes add
  CreationAliasCapabilityInterface, so
  DrupalBackend provides 34 and DrushBackend 14.
  Only a few edges are drawn here. A backend
  declares a capability only when it serves
  every method of it, so what only the
  in-process backend can do sits on a
  capability of its own, such as
  QueueItemCapabilityInterface.

  CoreCapabilityInterface hands out the core
  through getCore(), so no step resolves it:
  the layer lint rejects it under src/Steps.

  The root of src/Backend references no Drupal
  class; everything that is Drupal's sits under
  Backend\\Drupal. BackendRegistry walks the
  scenario's backend order and returns the first
  instance of the capability a step asked for,
  bootstrapping only that one.
end note
@enduml
